  "note": "The corpus calls the reduplicated passive Pulal, represented by polal here. Joel 1:10 and Nahum 1:4 are also indexed under the adjective because their spelling coincides. Lane p. 99 أَمَلَهُ means to hope. Oracc’s ummulu entries describe something stifled or faintly shining. Neither establishes a cognate for the Hebrew sense."
